        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 24 at 2:58PM EDT until September 25 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, northeast winds 25 to 35 kt with
gusts up to 45 kt and seas 13 to 16 feet. For the Storm
Warning, north winds 35 to 45 kt with gusts up to 60 kt and
seas 15 to 20 feet expected.

* WHERE...Waters from Sandy Hook NJ to Montauk Point NY from 20
to 60 nm.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 AM EDT Friday. For the
Storm Warning, from 6 AM Friday to 2 AM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Storm force winds and hazardous seas will capsize or
damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should remain in port, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for severe conditions.</instruction>
